course: dictionary
lesson: 4734
title: Words made of parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Hornless is made of horn and -less. The ending -less means without, so hornless means without horns. «That was Paraceratherium, a hornless relative of rhinos» tells you it had no horns.
explain: Use the swap test to check your meaning. Put «without horns» in place of hornless: «a without-horns relative of rhinos» is clumsy, but it still makes sense, so you know you are right.
explain: Context also tells you what kind of thing has no horns. «Hornless cattle», «a hornless goat» and «a hornless breed» are all animals. Some cattle, goats and sheep are naturally hornless, and some are bred that way for safety.
fact: Hornless means having no horns.
fact: The ending -less means without, so horn + less = without horns.
fact: Common phrases are «hornless cattle», «hornless goat» and «a hornless breed».
fact: Some cattle, goats and sheep are naturally hornless, and some are bred that way for safety.
fact: «Paraceratherium» was a hornless rhino that lived in Asia, including China, about 30 million years ago.
exercise: «Paraceratherium, a hornless rhino of Asia, was about 5 metres tall at the shoulder.» What does hornless mean? | Having very big horns | Having horns made of wood | *Having no horns | Having a long, curly tail
exercise: A farmer says, «Our goats are hornless, so they are safer.» What does hornless tell you about the goats? | They are made of horn | They can fly | They have two horns each | *They have no horns
exercise: «After the dinosaurs, the world grew new giants: ... a hornless rhino as heavy as several elephants.» Find and copy one word that means without horns. | giants | *hornless | heavy | elephants
test: What is a hornless goat? | A goat with two long horns | A goat that flies over the fields | A goat made of horn | *A goat with no horns
test: The ending -less in a word means? | Very | *Without | Before | Again
exam: Which phrase means the same as hornless? | Horned and fierce | Full of horns | *Without horns | With two horns
